Spring Boot Actuator exposes operational endpoints for monitoring, health checks, and management. Key endpoints: `/actuator/health` shows application health (UP/DOWN) — used by K8s liveness and readiness probes. `/actuator/health/liveness` returns whether the app is alive. `/actuator/health/readiness` returns whether the app is ready to accept traffic. `/actuator/prometheus` exposes metrics in Prometheus format (counter, gauge, histogram) — scraped by Prometheus, visualized in Grafana. `/actuator/loggers` allows RUNTIME log level changes without restart — change ERROR to DEBUG for a specific package during production troubleshooting.

```java
// Custom HealthIndicator — check business-critical dependency:
@Component
public class CoreBankingHealthIndicator implements HealthIndicator {
    @Override
    public Health health() {
        boolean coreUp = coreBankingClient.ping();
        return coreUp ? Health.up().withDetail("core", "reachable").build()
                       : Health.down().withDetail("core", "unreachable").build();
    }
}
// /actuator/health → includes custom check. If core banking is down → overall status DOWN.
```

Custom metrics with Micrometer: `meterRegistry.counter("trades.settled").increment()` creates a counter visible in Prometheus. `Timer.builder("trade.processing").register(registry)` measures processing duration. These metrics feed into Grafana dashboards for real-time monitoring.

```yaml
# Expose specific endpoints:
management:
  endpoints:
    web:
      exposure:
        include: health, prometheus, loggers, info
  server:
    port: 9092  # separate port for management (not exposed to public)
  health:
    probes:
      enabled: true  # /health/liveness and /health/readiness
```

